WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:25.710
The Umbrella by Claire Harris

00:25.760 --> 00:27.630
It is raining.

00:27.680 --> 00:30.750
The sky is grey.

00:30.800 --> 00:33.990
Carla goes to the market.

00:34.040 --> 00:36.710
She looks at the Umbrella's.

00:36.760 --> 00:39.550
She likes a red Umbrella.

00:39.600 --> 00:41.950
It's very smart.

00:42.000 --> 00:45.470
It costs ten dollars.

00:45.520 --> 00:48.070
Carla is a student.

00:48.120 --> 00:51.510
She doesn't have much money.

00:51.560 --> 00:55.510
I can give you seven dollars for that Umbrella.

00:55.560 --> 00:57.710
OK, young lady.

00:57.760 --> 01:00.470
This is your lucky day.

01:00.520 --> 01:02.630
Give me seven dollars.

01:02.680 --> 01:07.070
The Umbrella is yours.

01:07.120 --> 01:11.910
This is my lucky day. Says Carla.

01:11.960 --> 01:16.030
She holds the red Umbrella above her head.

01:16.080 --> 01:20.470
The rain falls on the Umbrella.

01:20.520 --> 01:23.790
Carla goes to a cake shop.

01:23.840 --> 01:26.670
She wants to buy some cakes.

01:26.720 --> 01:30.590
Her little brother loves cakes.

01:30.640 --> 01:33.110
She goes into the shop.

01:33.160 --> 01:38.270
She leaves her red Umbrella near the door.

01:38.320 --> 01:41.870
It is quiet inside the shop.

01:41.920 --> 01:45.750
Carla chooses three small cakes.

01:45.800 --> 01:49.550
She talks to the shop assistant.

01:49.600 --> 01:52.790
A customer is leaving the shop.

01:52.840 --> 01:55.510
She is a young woman.

01:55.560 --> 01:59.830
She is holding a cake box.

01:59.880 --> 02:03.190
Carla is going to leave the shop.

02:03.240 --> 02:07.230
But where is her Umbrella?

02:07.280 --> 02:10.630
There is one Umbrella near the door.

02:10.680 --> 02:14.110
It is not a red Umbrella.

02:14.160 --> 02:18.070
It is not Carla's Umbrella.

02:18.120 --> 02:22.630
This Umbrella is old and black.

02:22.680 --> 02:26.070
It has a pattern of yellow ducks.

02:26.120 --> 02:28.510
It is not smart.

02:28.560 --> 02:30.080
Carla takes the Umbrella.

02:33.920 --> 02:37.950
This is not my lucky day.

02:38.000 --> 02:41.630
Carla walks to the town square.

02:41.680 --> 02:44.830
A young man speaks to her.

02:44.880 --> 02:47.310
Hello?

02:47.360 --> 02:49.070
He smiles.

02:49.120 --> 02:52.710
Carla does not know this young man.

02:52.760 --> 02:56.590
She walks away quickly.

02:56.640 --> 03:00.350
The young man is following Carla.

03:00.400 --> 03:04.070
She walks into a crowd of people.

03:04.120 --> 03:08.950
The young man follows the black and yellow Umbrella.

03:09.000 --> 03:10.470
Hello?

03:10.520 --> 03:12.590
Wait!

03:12.640 --> 03:15.110
Carla turns.

03:15.160 --> 03:18.030
She looks at the young man.

03:18.080 --> 03:19.910
She is angry.

03:19.960 --> 03:23.550
Go away. She says.

03:23.600 --> 03:26.270
The young man is sad.

03:26.320 --> 03:28.550
Marisa, I'm sorry.

03:28.600 --> 03:32.510
He says, I'm very late.

03:32.560 --> 03:36.750
I'm not Marisa. Carla shouts.

03:36.800 --> 03:41.390
You are not Marisa, says the young man.

03:41.440 --> 03:45.870
He points at the black Umbrella with yellow ducks.

03:45.920 --> 03:48.430
That's her Umbrella.

03:48.480 --> 03:51.790
Oh. Says Carla.

03:51.840 --> 03:54.830
Who is Marisa?

03:54.880 --> 03:59.270
I don't know Marisa, says the young man.

03:59.320 --> 04:02.110
I'm going to meet her.

04:02.160 --> 04:05.510
We are going to have coffee.

04:05.560 --> 04:08.790
It is my cousin's idea.

04:08.840 --> 04:12.110
Marisa works with my cousin.

04:12.160 --> 04:17.630
I am not Marisa. Says Carla again.

04:17.680 --> 04:22.910
My cousin has a photo of Marisa, says the young man.

04:22.960 --> 04:24.870
She's tall.

04:24.920 --> 04:26.910
You're tall.

04:26.960 --> 04:30.430
Her hair is short and dark.

04:30.480 --> 04:34.270
Your hair is short and dark.

04:34.320 --> 04:37.990
In the photo, she has an Umbrella.

04:38.040 --> 04:43.070
It's a black Umbrella with yellow ducks.

04:43.120 --> 04:46.720
You have a black Umbrella with yellow ducks.

04:50.320 --> 04:54.310
Carla looks up at the old Umbrella.

04:54.360 --> 04:57.790
Marisa is a thief. She thinks.

04:57.840 --> 05:01.270
She has my new red Umbrella.

05:01.320 --> 05:05.230
Carla is angry again.

05:05.280 --> 05:10.590
Please don't be angry, says the young man.

05:10.640 --> 05:13.230
He looks at his watch.

05:13.280 --> 05:15.670
It's 3 o'clock.

05:15.720 --> 05:20.070
Marisa goes to work at 2.30.

05:20.120 --> 05:22.670
I can't meet her now.

05:22.720 --> 05:25.350
It's too late.

05:25.400 --> 05:28.470
He smiles at Carla.

05:28.520 --> 05:33.310
Let's have coffee together, he says.

05:33.360 --> 05:36.510
Carla thinks for a moment.

05:36.560 --> 05:38.990
OK. She says.

05:39.040 --> 05:42.310
Let's go to my aunt's cafe.

05:42.360 --> 05:45.270
The young man smiles again.

05:45.320 --> 05:50.030
That will be great, he says.

05:50.080 --> 05:52.950
My name is Paul.

05:53.000 --> 05:57.030
I'm a law student, third year.

05:57.080 --> 05:58.910
I'm Carla.

05:58.960 --> 06:00.990
I'm a student, too.

06:01.040 --> 06:02.270
I'm studying science.

06:02.320 --> 06:07.270
Carla sits in the cafe with Paul.

06:07.320 --> 06:10.270
They drink coffee.

06:10.320 --> 06:12.270
They talk.

06:12.320 --> 06:14.270
They laugh.

06:14.320 --> 06:18.270
They laugh and talk.

06:18.320 --> 06:22.270
Suddenly, Carla jumps up.

06:22.320 --> 06:25.270
Oh, no! She says.

06:25.320 --> 06:26.270
It's late.

06:26.320 --> 06:28.270
I must go home.

06:28.320 --> 06:30.270
I'm a study.

06:30.320 --> 06:35.270
I'm going to have an exam tomorrow.

06:35.320 --> 06:38.270
Good luck.

06:38.320 --> 06:40.270
Will you meet me again?

06:40.320 --> 06:41.270
Yes.

06:41.320 --> 06:45.270
That will be nice.

06:45.320 --> 06:48.270
It is almost dark.

06:48.320 --> 06:52.270
The town square is quiet.

06:52.320 --> 06:57.270
Carla sees a tall young woman.

06:57.320 --> 07:02.270
The young woman has short, dark hair.

07:02.320 --> 07:06.270
She has a smart umbrella.

07:06.320 --> 07:09.270
It is a red umbrella.

07:09.320 --> 07:14.270
The young woman is Marisa.

07:14.320 --> 07:20.270
Marisa sees the old black umbrella with yellow ducks.

07:20.320 --> 07:23.270
She is worried.

07:23.320 --> 07:27.270
Suddenly, her face is red.

07:27.320 --> 07:30.270
Don't worry, says Carla.

07:30.320 --> 07:32.270
Keep my red umbrella.

07:32.320 --> 07:35.270
I like this umbrella.

07:35.320 --> 07:37.270
It's a lucky umbrella.

07:37.320 --> 07:40.270
This is my lucky day.

07:40.320 --> 07:44.270
The rain falls on the umbrellas.

07:44.320 --> 07:46.270
Carla smiles.

07:46.320 --> 07:50.320
Then, she runs home.

07:53.320 --> 07:58.320
MUSIC
